{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Counting and Inventory","anchor":"Counting-and-Inventory","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units\/Count","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/baseCount()"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Counting Units for Inventory and Blending","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"role":"article"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CountingUnits"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create unlimited, identifiable dimensionless units for counting eggs, apples,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bottles, cases, and anything else your point-of-sale or inventory app tracks."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/countingunits"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some quantities are measured; others are counted. A recipe uses 3 eggs, a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carton holds 12, and a case holds 360. Counts are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"dimensionless","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"—they have no"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"meters, grams, or seconds—but they still need identity: eggs and apples are not"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"interchangeable just because both are dimensionless."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CountUnit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a runtime-extensible count unit. There is no fixed catalog, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can create as many item-specific count units as your app needs:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Math","","let egg = CountUnit(item: \"egg\")","let dozenEggs = CountUnit(item: \"egg\", symbol: \"doz\", factor: 12)","let caseOfEggs = CountUnit(item: \"egg\", symbol: \"case\", factor: 360)","","let apple = CountUnit(item: \"apple\")","let caseOfApples = CountUnit(item: \"apple\", symbol: \"case\", factor: 120)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every count unit is still dimensionless, so it works with the rest of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"per-count prices, ratios, blending, and inventory totals.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Quick-start","text":"Quick start","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Math","","\/\/ 1. Create item-specific count units at runtime.","let egg = CountUnit(item: \"egg\")","let dozenEggs = CountUnit(item: \"egg\", symbol: \"doz\", factor: 12)","let caseOfEggs = CountUnit(item: \"egg\", symbol: \"case\", factor: 360)","","\/\/ 2. Count quantities.","let carton = Quantity(value: 2, unit: dozenEggs)","let loose = Quantity(value: 5, unit: egg)","","\/\/ 3. Convert within the same item family.","carton.converted(to: egg) \/\/ 24 egg","carton.baseCount()        \/\/ 24 egg","","\/\/ 4. Blend counts; the right-hand side converts to the left-hand unit.","let total = loose + carton                     \/\/ 29 egg","let inCartons = total.converted(to: dozenEggs) \/\/ 2.4166... doz","","\/\/ 5. Price per count; the count cancels and leaves currency.","let pricePerEgg = Quantity(value: 0.25, unit: Units.usd.per(egg))","let cost = pricePerEgg * carton \/\/ $6.00","","\/\/ 6. Generic scales act as wildcards.","let pricePerDozen = Quantity(value: 3.00, unit: Units.usd.per(Units.Count.dozen))","pricePerDozen * carton \/\/ $6.00","","\/\/ 7. Generic counts and leading-dot lookup.","let dozens = Quantity(value: 2, unit: .dozen)","dozens.converted(to: .each) 